      "message": "\u003e +1, but I think we should be careful not to overstate the impact. \n\nAgreed, hence a P3. I don\u0027t believe there is any exposure of sensitive data to any authorised user. This is more of a compliance issue, as it logs credentials in clear text, which violates security policies.\n\n\u003e Assuming these logs are only accessible to an admin, that admin already has the ability to impersonate a user through `suexec` and `X-Run-As` capabilities (with some subtle differences). IIUC, the credential scope here is only valid for Gerrit.\n\nExactly, P3 is more for breaking compliance.",
